Well, when I was reading this section of the text, I instantly thought of M.C. Escher, specifically that famous lithograph ascending and descending, where the monks are walking on a staircase on top of a monastery.

22:09.880 --> 22:10.900
The Penrose stairs.

22:11.280 --> 22:19.680
Right. If you look at that drawing locally, like if you tile it and just examine one monk taking one single step, the geometry is perfectly valid.

22:19.680 --> 22:21.260
It's a locally coherent tile.

22:21.560 --> 22:21.800
Yes.

