In Flyxion's framework, that continuous upwards loop is called a topological obstruction.

22:49.340 --> 22:51.140
A topological obstruction.

22:51.380 --> 22:55.200
It isn't a small numerical error that you can fix by tweaking an algorithm.

22:55.960 --> 23:00.780
The local rules are fundamentally irreducibly at war with the global architecture.

23:01.380 --> 23:03.000
You cannot glue the tiles together.

23:03.320 --> 23:08.120
In Flyxion gives a specific term for what happens to a model when it hits this obstruction.

23:08.500 --> 23:08.800
Yes.

